prompt:
You are a sceptical financial analyst reviewing a forecast prepared by a colleague.

Given the following forecast for NTPC (base year 2021):
{
  "strategy": "baseline",
  "base_year": 2021,
  "forecast": [
    {
      "year": 2022,
      "revenue_cr": 117136.08,
      "net_income_cr": 15706.67,
      "eps": 15.96
    },
    {
      "year": 2023,
      "revenue_cr": 122985.03,
      "net_income_cr": 16481.05,
      "eps": 16.75
    },
    {
      "year": 2024,
      "revenue_cr": 129125.06,
      "net_income_cr": 17298.93,
      "eps": 17.58
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": "From the Consolidated P&L, Revenue from Operations was \u20b91,11,531.15 crore in FY2021 vs \u20b91,09,464.04 crore in FY2020, implying a YoY revenue growth of ~1.89%. Net Income (Profit for the year) was \u20b914,969.40 crore in FY2021 vs \u20b911,901.98 crore in FY2020, implying a YoY net income growth of ~25.77%; however, this was significantly boosted by a lower effective tax rate (normalisation from the anomalously high FY2020 tax expense of \u20b99,347.54 crore), so a moderated net income growth rate of ~4.92% (average of revenue and raw PAT growth, reflecting normalisation) is used for forward projections. Shares outstanding (weighted average) as reported for EPS calculation is approximately 984.47 crore shares, used consistently for FY2022\u20132024 EPS estimates."
}

Step 1: Identify the 3 most critical assumptions embedded in this forecast.
Step 2: For each assumption, describe one plausible scenario where it fails.
Step 3: Rate each assumption failure as Low / Medium / High risk to the forecast accuracy.
Step 4: Assign an overall confidence score from 0-100 (100 = completely certain).

RESPONSE FORMAT: Begin your response DIRECTLY with the opening brace { — no reasoning or text before the JSON.

Return ONLY valid JSON:
{
  "company": "<COMPANY>",
  "base_year": <YYYY>,
  "strategy": "<baseline|alt_strategy>",
  "assumptions": [
    {"assumption": "<text>", "failure_scenario": "<text>", "risk": "<Low|Medium|High>"}
  ],
  "confidence_score": <0-100>,
  "overall_critique": "<2 sentences>"
}

